# The Product Knowledge database is shipped with the code: it is a versioned,
# read-only knowledge source built by a separate project, not runtime state,
# and the server needs it to answer product-specification questions. This is
# the ONLY database that belongs in the repository -- the operational DB, its
# WAL/SHM sidecars and every backup stay excluded by the rules above, so a
# deploy can never overwrite the server's live data with a development copy.
!data/product_facts.db

data/backups/
data/dps_agent_state.json
data/dps_connection.json
data/dps_windows_cache.json
data/chrome*/
data/*cookie*.json
data/*session*.json
chrome-profile/
chrome_profile/
user-data-dir/

